# Helter Skelter, intro (figure 150.1): twelve bars over a descending chromatic line
# The rows of the second system are unlabeled; they continue Pollack's three rows (Upper voice 1,
# Upper voice 2, Chords). Upper voice 2 carries the downward chromatic line D C# C B to G#; its D
# under the E chord is the 4/2 seventh, and its C# under A the 6/3.
# The pickup note before bar 1 and the vocal's entry (a pickup to bar 3) are not in the chart.
#? Octaves (upper voice 1 at E4, voice 2 from D4 down to G#3, meeting in unison on C4 in bar 7) are a guess; check the register of these lines on the record.
